---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MortgageRecastCalculator from "../../../components/MortgageRecastCalculator.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Australia Mortgage Recast & Offset Calculator | ASIC Moneysmart Rules"
  description="Explore Australian home loan lump-sum payment options, offset account benefits, and redraw recalculation scenarios."
  ogImage="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/images/og-home.png"
>
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/mortgage-recast-calculator/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-us" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/mortgage-recast-calculator/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-ca" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/mortgage-recast-calculator/canada/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-gb" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/mortgage-recast-calculator/uk/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-au" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/mortgage-recast-calculator/australia/" slot="head" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "FinanceApplication",
        "name": "Australia Mortgage Recast & Offset Calculator",
        "applicationCategory": "FinanceApplication",
        "operatingSystem": "Web",
        "provider": {
          "@id": "https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/#organization"
        },
        "offers": {
          "@type": "Offer",
          "price": "0",
          "priceCurrency": "AUD"
        },
        "description": "Model Australian home loan repayment reductions following lump-sum payments and offset strategy comparisons."
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Can Australian home loans be recast?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Formal 'recasting' as known in the US does not exist as a named product in Australia. Australian borrowers instead use offset accounts — where savings held in a linked transaction account reduce the loan balance on which interest is calculated — and redraw facilities, which let you access extra repayments you've already made. Both achieve a similar interest-saving effect without requiring a formal loan modification."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How does a mortgage offset account work in Australia?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "A 100% offset account is a transaction account linked to your home loan. The balance in this account is offset against your outstanding loan principal when calculating interest. For example, if you owe $400,000 and have $50,000 in your offset account, you only pay interest on $350,000. The money remains accessible at any time, giving you flexibility that a direct lump-sum repayment does not."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is the difference between an offset account and a redraw facility?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "An offset account is a separate transaction account whose balance reduces the interest charged on your home loan; the funds remain yours and are instantly accessible. A redraw facility lets you access extra repayments you've already made on the loan itself, but availability and processing times vary by lender. The key distinction is that offset funds never actually reduce your loan balance — they just reduce the interest calculation — while redraw involves money that has already been applied to the principal."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>

  <main class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <div class="mb-8 text-center sm:text-left">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight font-sans">
        Australia Mortgage Recast & Offset Calculator
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400 max-w-3xl">
        Model home loan principal reductions, compare Mortgage Offset vs. Redraw, and calculate monthly payment adjustments.
      </p>
    </div>

    <MortgageRecastCalculator country="australia" />

    <!-- Explanatory Content Wrapper -->
    <div class="mt-12 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
      <!-- Introduction Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#00F5D4]/10 text-[#00F5D4] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#00F5D4]/20">
          <span>Australian Home Loan Framework</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Introduction</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          "Mortgage recasting" — the US mechanism where you pay a lump sum and the lender formally recalculates your monthly payment at the same rate and term — is not a named product in the Australian home loan market. Instead, Australian borrowers primarily reduce their interest costs through <strong>offset accounts</strong> and <strong>redraw facilities</strong>, both of which are widely offered by Australian lenders. A 100% offset account is a transaction account linked to your home loan: the balance in the offset is subtracted from your outstanding loan principal before interest is calculated, so $50,000 sitting in your offset on a $400,000 loan means you only pay interest on $350,000 — while the money remains fully accessible. A redraw facility, by contrast, lets you make extra repayments directly onto the loan and later withdraw ("redraw") them if needed, though lender policies on access vary. This calculator models the interest-saving effect of deploying a lump sum via either strategy, so you can quantify how much you save compared to the standard repayment schedule and make an informed decision about where to park spare cash.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Key Benefits Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#7B61FF]/10 text-[#7B61FF] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#7B61FF]/20">
          <span>Strategic Value</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Key Benefits</h2>
        <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Model Offset Account Impact</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">See how parking savings in a 100% offset account reduces the balance on which interest is calculated, lowering total interest costs.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Compare Offset vs. Redraw</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Evaluate whether the flexibility of an offset account outweighs the potential fee savings of a basic loan with redraw.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Quantify Lifetime Interest Savings</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Calculate the total interest you avoid paying over the remaining loan term by deploying a lump sum now rather than keeping it in a standard savings account.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Estimate Term Reduction</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Project how many years sooner you could pay off your home loan by making extra repayments or maintaining an offset balance.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Retain Liquidity</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Unlike a US recast where the lump sum is permanently applied to principal, an Australian offset lets you access the funds anytime while still saving on interest.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#00F5D4]/10 text-[#00F5D4] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#00F5D4]/20">
          <span>Common Questions</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] overflow-hidden">
            <button 
              type="button"
              onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden'); this.querySelector('svg').classList.toggle('rotate-180');" 
